PATCH 630: restore byte storage and the initial mode-1 mixer setup (board:0003).

Original 23ee MOV AL,[2293] and 2496 MOV [2293],BL access one byte.
The generated DWORD accessor includes the following 2294 RET opcode and
therefore invokes the previous-mode callback even with original mode zero;
its DWORD store also overwrites the following three code bytes.

Original 2485 is E8 A6 01 00 00, a direct CALL 2630. Resolve it to the existing
translated mixer, whose normalization, byte writes and rollover callback
contracts are already owned by patches 622-624. The generated placeholder
returns without producing the initial DMA half or advancing channel state.

A paired read-only original capture brackets actual first 23ec/AL=1 through
138d before CLI changes IF. The complete independent 534:536-ms trace is
byte-identical to the earlier unprobed source: 45185 prefix instructions,
1024 mixer stores, one rollover and no channel callback. All 39 frames,
27518 mixed samples and the complete 600-ms endpoint retain their bytes.
The tracked fixture records all 18 changed module bytes, both DMA halves,
actual mode tables and complete neighboring instructions. It supplies no
elapsed delay. tools/oracle/initial_mixer_call_case.json holds provenance.

The regression compiles the complete ordered-patched module and enters the
real 23ec with original AX=4e01. The test stops when it dispatches 138d,
without replacing or accepting that unimplemented device initializer.
Every other indirect target fails. Parent native/WASM instead dispatch 2294
because of the wrong-width initial mode read. With that width corrected
alone, both reach 138d but still omit the original mixer state changes.
The next reaching failure is the shared rollover-parameter storage: original
2507/250e/2515/251c/2523/252a write six separate BYTE values at 1613..1618.
The generated DWORD writes at 1617/1618 erase the mixer counter's low bytes
at 1619/161a after its 1024 stores. Correct the shared six accessors to BYTE,
also retaining original 2394/23a3 byte-indexed queued-channel stores and
rollover reads. The read-only paired state proves counter 00010400, while
both targets with only mode/call corrected retain 00010000. Original bytes
and this intermediate reaching failure remain in initial-mixer-call/.

Compare the entire isolated one-MiB module and all 2048 DMA bytes; code next
to 2293 must remain unchanged. Actual startup integration, device/IRQ/IF,
guest stacks, instruction timing and final PCM remain open.
